issue(id="0012" status="closed")
  title Align the HTML converter with formatter settings and shared text layout logic
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of puggers
    i-want the HTML converter to honor formatter settings intentionally and start sharing the layout code that those settings drive
    so-that imported output and formatted output stop drifting for the same width, indentation, and text-layout decisions
  premise.
    Task `0007` establishes baseline corrections for importer behavior, while
    tasks `0010` and `0011` are intended to clarify whitespace policy
    boundaries. Once those semantics are stable enough, the next step is to
    make the converter intentionally compatible with formatter settings instead
    of growing a second mostly-similar behavior matrix. That work should start
    code sharing in earnest where the logic is already converging: width-aware
    text layout, prose reflow, indentation width, tab handling, and any
    attribute or quote-style rendering that genuinely means the same thing on
    both sides. The goal is not to force the importer and formatter into the
    same architecture, but to extract the shared policy and rendering pieces
    that would otherwise drift. This task should also give us a more explicit
    compatibility register, closer in spirit to the vendored-fixture inventory
    work elsewhere in the repo, so we can see which formatter settings already
    line up, which are intentionally importer-only, and which still need
    alignment.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Define which formatter settings the converter should honor as true compatibility settings versus which remain importer-specific controls, and document that boundary.
    criterion Begin sharing at least one meaningful text-layout or rendering component between the converter and formatter rather than only mirroring behavior in parallel implementations.
    criterion Add tests that show matching settings produce intentionally aligned output decisions for width, indentation, and at least one other shared formatting concern.
    criterion Add an explicit compatibility inventory or behavior register that shows which formatter settings currently align with converter behavior and which remain out of scope or pending.
    criterion Keep importer-only extraction behavior separate enough that shared code does not absorb DOM-selection or HTML-specific policy decisions.
    criterion Document the initial shared-core boundary so later compatibility work can extend it without reintroducing drift by accident.
  review-items
    item(status="covered") The first compatibility tranche covers `lineWidth`, `indentWidth`, `useTabs`, and `quoteStyle` through `puggers-core::PugFormatOptions`.
    item(status="covered") The shared component is now code-backed: indentation, display width, prose word wrapping, and quoted attribute rendering live in `puggers-core`.
    item(status="covered") Compatibility inventory is documented in `docs/importer-formatter-compatibility.md` and backed by focused cross-surface tests.
    item(status="covered") Importer-only extraction controls remain on `ConvertOptions` outside the shared formatting option type.
    item(status="covered") Review accepted the pre-1.0 `ConvertOptions::formatting` API change and confirmed `quoteStyle` as a fully shared puggers ecosystem option; wasm diagnostic dead-code cleanup is intentionally separate future work.
